MIFM1's changes to fm1-base (base/), applied by tools/patch_base.sh before a build.
(0.16.53) The screen mirror (device/mirror.c, fm1.toml mirror = true) for a UI drawn in tiles, not only in full rows:
fm1-base's kept a row's segments (30 px) only for blits the screen's whole width, and took a row for right again
only when one came whole; MIFM1 draws its knobs in 60-pixel tiles, so their rows stayed wrong for good, the UI was
asked to draw everything again 20 times a second, and each time the ring was full before the last knobs and the
footer: the viewer never had them. Now each segment of each row is known or not, wrong or not (mr.kn, mr.dt: a byte a
row, 480 B for the 64 of the two bitmaps): a blit on the segments' bounds (x and w multiples of 30) is compared and
sent segment by segment as a full row was; another one sent whole, the segments it covers whole known and right after
it, the ones it covers in part unknown; a part dropped makes the segments it touches wrong. And plat_mirroring()
(0: no host; else 1 + the room in the ring, only 1 while a dropped part waits): what moves on its own (MIFM1's LFO
scope) drawn when there is room, after the rest. The protocol and the viewers unchanged.
Checked: fm1-base's tests/mirror_test.c (its internals' names changed): the same checks pass as before (its session's
check fails here before as after, with this fm1-base), and MIFM1's firmware/tests/mirror.txt with
tools/mirror_check.py (make mirror-check): each session's screen whole at the viewer, every pixel.

